Revision history for Cooklang

2.1.0   2026-10-14 12:53:01 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Align with the current Cooklang spec tests (t/spec submodule)
 - Optional ingredients and cookware: @?name, #?name
 - Front matter is parsed as YAML (YAMLish is now a dependency)
 - Scaling: fixed quantities {=1%tsp}, cookware and timers are not scaled,
   and new 'servings' attribute to scale to a number of servings
 - cook() returns the original recipe text
 - human(): better plurals and a/an, optional items marked
 - Throw Cooklang::ParseError when a recipe can not be parsed
 - Fix metadata keys spanning lines, block comment values and Measurement methods
 - Ranges like {2-3} are scaled at both ends; whole numbers are shown as 8, not 8.0
 - human() leaves out the '\' that marks a line break
 - Notes ('> text') and sections ('== Dough =='), with new notes() and sections() methods
 - human(): cookware without a given quantity is shown without one, one line per metadata
 - Tests with the spec example recipes and made-up recipes using all features
 - Clearer grammar, more tests and updated documentation

2.0.1   2024-10-29 16:45:00 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Restructure data into objects for better flexibility

1.1.1   2023-08-10 15:17:30 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Add qamount note

1.1.0   2023-08-04 13:04:10 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Renamed .ast to .data, as it does not return an AST tree.
 - Added parsing for '//' modifiier.

1.0.6   2023-08-04 09:42:30 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Improved match where it could fail to match recipe

1.0.5   2023-08-01 13:15:00 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Accept list of .cook files

1.0.3   2023-08-01 11:00:00 Europe/Copenhagen
 - Update POD6.

1.0.2   2023-07-31 14:59:12 Europe/Copenhagen
 - First version. Passes all tests.
